,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":587.7535844,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":587.753585484,"data":"--- [algebra.factoring.simon_factoring_trick] ---\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":587.753586765,"data":"Triggers: Diophantine equation with cross term xy and linear terms, xy + ax + by = c, need integer solutions of bilinear equation\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":587.753588188,"data":"Technique: Simon's Favorite Factoring Trick (SFFT): xy + ax + by + ab = (x+b)(y+a). Add ab to both sides of xy+ax+by=c to get (x+b)(y+a)=c+ab. Then enumerate factor pairs of c+ab. Works for any bilinear Diophantine equation.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":587.753590514,"data":"Question: Find all positive integer solutions to xy + 3x + 2y = 55.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":587.753591987,"data":"Answer: Add 6 to both sides: xy + 3x + 2y + 6 = 61. Factor: (x+2)(y+3) = 61. Since 61 is prime and x,y\u003e0: x+2\u003e2 and y+3\u003e3, so x+2=61, y+3=1 (impossible since y\u003e0) or x+2=1 (impossible since x\u003e0). Actually with positive integers: (x+2)(y+3)=61, factors of 61: 1*61 or 61*1. x+2=61=\u003ex=59,y+3=1=\u003ey=-2 (invalid). x+2=1=\u003ex=-1 (invalid). So no positive integer solutions. For non-prime RHS, enumerate all factor pairs.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":587.753594784,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":587.753595921,"data":"[END EXPERT NOTES]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":587.753597101,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":587.753598184,"data":"Our IMO expert has also shared his special notes database. If you are stuck or want more hints, query it:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":587.753599488,"data":"import sqlite3; db = sqlite3.connect(\"/kaggle/input/aimo3-problem-db/problems.db\")\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":587.753600935,"data":"Schema: id, category, topic, subtopic, taxonomy, triggers, technique, question, answer\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":587.753602216,"data":"db.execute(\"SELECT taxonomy, triggers, technique FROM problems WHERE category=?\", (CATEGORY,)).fetchall()\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":587.753603721,"data":"Find the closest match, then read the full approach:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":587.753604946,"data":"db.execute(\"SELECT technique, question, answer FROM problems WHERE taxonomy=?\", (TAX,)).fetchone()\n"}
